skills.inject:
Grotto Runtime SDK — the Grotto host provides trusted identity, cloud saves, events and leaderboards. Wire it, and DEGRADE GRACEFULLY (localStorage / no-ops) when `window.GrottoRuntime` is absent so the game still runs standalone:
  const grotto = await window.GrottoRuntime?.ready?.({ timeoutMs: 8000 }).catch(() => null);
  const player = grotto && await grotto.getPlayer();          // trusted host identity
  const save = grotto ? await grotto.loadSave('default', DEFAULT_STATE) : { state: DEFAULT_STATE };
  await grotto?.save('default', state);                       // cloud autosave
  await grotto?.submitScore(score, { board: 'default' });     // server keeps best
  const top = await grotto?.leaderboard({ board: 'default', limit: 10 });
Never ask the client to prove identity. `inventory:read` and `multiplayer:join` exist only for exact game IDs enabled by platform policy. Runtime wallet authority is an immutable private launch snapshot, and heartbeats never exceed the 24-hour absolute session lifetime. Multiplayer uses a fresh one-use ticket for every connect/reconnect; `roomId=public` is routing only, not match authorization.
